      "text": "We first square the vector equation given, $\\mathbf{w} \\times \\mathbf{u} = \\mathbf{v},$ to get that\n$$(\\mathbf{w} \\times \\mathbf{u}) \\cdot (\\mathbf{w} \\times \\mathbf{u}) = \\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}.$$\nExpanding the left side, using the distributive property on the vectors, and the fact that $\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = 1,$ we get that\n$$\\mathbf{w} \\cdot (\\mathbf{w} \\times \\mathbf{u}) \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = 1.$$\nSince $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{w} \\times \\mathbf{u},$ this shows that\n$$\\mathbf{w} = \\mathbf{0}.$$\nTherefore, $\\mathbf{v} \\times \\mathbf{w} = \\mathbf{0},$ so $\\mathbf{u} \\cdot (\\mathbf{v} \\times \\mathbf{w}) = \\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{0} = \\boxed{0}.$. The answer is 0",
